      "summary": "Sparse accessor references are checked for valid bufferView indices but not for in-range data. A malformed GLB can therefore pass validation and reach the injected renderer loader.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "frontend/src/hangar/glbValidator.ts",
          "line": 191,
          "message": "Sparse accessor byte ranges are not validated, allowing out-of-range data to pass the validation boundary.",
          "confidence": 0.92,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Sparse accessor validation checks only that the indices and values reference an existing bufferView. It does not check their byte offsets or ranges against that view before loadValidatedHangarAsset invokes the renderer loader.",
            "failureScenario": "A GLB with a 24-byte bufferView and a sparse accessor whose indices and values both specify byteOffset 100 passes validation. The boundary then passes those malformed bytes to the injected loader, which may read sparse data outside the validated view. OWASP A06:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
